Trick: Zeek is Big picture, Arkime  search, Wireshark depth analysis for specific packet.

## As analyst step by step (on honeypot example)

Maan lo aapko jaanna hai ki **date 10 ko honeypot 1 par kya hua** .

| Step | Kya karte ho                                                                        | Kaun sa tool                                           |
|:----:|:------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|:-------------------------------------------------------|
| 1    | Poore din ka summary: kaun se IP ne sabse zyada connection kiye, kaun se ports par  | **Zeek** (`conn.log`) ya **Elasticsearch** me search   |
| 2    | Suspicious IP mila, jaise `64.62.197.110`. Ab ye dekhna hai ki isne aur kya kiya    | **Arkime** (browser me `ip == 64.62.197.110`)          |
| 3    | Iske saare sessions ek jagah dikhte hain: kab aaya, kaun se ports, kya maanga       | **Arkime**                                             |
| 4    | Ek session ka gehra analysis chahiye: packets ke andar kya tha                      | **Arkime** se pcap download, phir **Wireshark** me kholo |
| 5    | Dusre honeypots ya dusre dino me ye IP dikha ya nahi                                | **Elasticsearch / Arkime** (sab ek jagah indexed)      |







=====================================================================================================================

## 6. Kab kaunsa tool chahiye

| Halat                                                          | Kya chahiye                                                                                           |
|:---------------------------------------------------------------|:------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Ek ya do pcap files hain, aur ek-ek packet dekhna hai          | **Wireshark**                                                                                         |
| Pcap files se jaldi summary chahiye (IPs, ports, HTTP requests) | **Zeek**                                                                                              |
| Bahut saari pcap files (date 10, 18, 25...), browser me search karni hain | **Arkime** (+ Elasticsearch)                                                                |
| Lakhon logs ko search aur graph me dekhna hai                  | **Elasticsearch + Kibana**                                                                            |
| Sab kuch ek saath, tayyar setup                                | **Malcolm** (Zeek, Arkime aur OpenSearch ko jodta hai). Isme pcap upload karne ke tareeke uske docs me dekhna |






------------------------------------------------------------------- Step by step guide to use Zeek and Arkime


- check docker is working or not  
      docker --version

- pull the zeek images
      docker pull zeek/zeek:lts

- Go to destination path and create Directory, and 
    cd C:\Users\P\Desktop\pcappapa\merged_output
    mkdir zeek_10_hp1
    docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/data" -w /data/zeek_10_hp1 zeek/zeek:lts zeek -C -r /data/10_cdac_hp_1.pcap

  
     Hissa                                                            	Matlab
     --rm	                                                     Kaam ke baad container hata do
     -v "${PWD}:/data"	                                       Aapka merged_output folder container ke andar /data bana do
     -w /data/zeek_10_hp1	                                     Zeek ko is folder me chalao (logs yahin banenge)
     zeek -r /data/10_cdac_hp_1.pcap	                         Zeek ko ye pcap padhne ko kaho
     -C	                                                       Checksum 

 Note:  -C kyun: Aapke Wireshark me Checksum: ... [unverified] dikha tha. Computer apni network card se capture karne par aksar checksum galat dikhta hai (hardware offload).
 Zeek by default aise packets ko kharab maan kar chhod deta hai. -C laga kar wo sab packets le leta hai.





















